- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/reactiondiffusion_block_end.html
- Summary (EN): Reaction-Diffusion Block End closes a Reaction-Diffusion simulation block and produces a 2D pattern from two chemicals that react and diffuse. It pairs with Reaction-Diffusion Block Begin, which provides the chemical input. The page body shows only the display name; the internal name is confirmed by the Copernicus nodes index entry.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud ferme un bloc de simulation Réaction-Diffusion et produit un motif 2D à partir de deux chimiques qui réagissent et diffusent.

- Inputs meaning: ["chemical: input chemical data from the Reaction-Diffusion Block Begin COP", "feedback: cable carrying the current feedback data, fed back into the simulation; its structure must match the initial structure set on the block begin"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: Pattern (Mono) for a remapped, corrected output, or Chemical (UV) for raw chemical values", "Model: Gray-Scott (two reaction parameters, Alpha/Feed and Beta/Kill) or Kenjiro Maginu (three reaction parameters, Alpha, Beta and Gamma)", "Preset: fills in reaction parameters for named pattern styles, such as Spots, Worms or Labyrinth for Gray-Scott", "Simulate: feeds outputs back into inputs for a feedback loop; Reset Simulation clears the cache", "Iterations and Iterations per Step: number of iterations in non-simulation mode and per step", "Live Simulation: interactive mode that runs independently of the playbar and is not cached", "Time Scale and Substeps: reaction speed and number of substeps per simulated frame", "Caching (Start Frame, Cached Frames, Checkpoint Rate): frame caching during Simulate", "Switch to Raw Values: off is recommended, so parameters are normalized to reduce instability", "Scale Multiplier: changes pattern size by adjusting the reaction rate relative to diffusion", "Diffusion A / Diffusion B: how fast each chemical diffuses; the two models use different typical ratios", "Boundary inputs (Invert Boundary, Boundary Threshold, Boundary Smoothing): shape growth within an SDF boundary", "Output Correction (Invert, Normalize Model, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum): active only with Pattern (Mono)"]

- Caveats: ["Compiled COP networks do not support simulation.", "The reaction is sensitive to parameter changes and can become unstable or die out.", "The solver is resolution-sensitive: doubling the resolution may require about four times the Substeps, or a quarter of the Time Scale.", "Live Simulation does not save results, so use a Stash COP to keep them; its caching parameters do not apply.", "Chemical (UV) output is raw and offers no colour control, so it may look unfriendly.", "The activation mask must sit inside a valid area of the boundary, or the reaction cannot grow.", "Alpha, beta and gamma inputs on the Block Begin COP override the matching parameters on this node."]

